; The extent of a masked access is measured from its enabled lanes, not from
; its vector type. Here the accumulator is the 3-lane prefix of a
; <4 x double> row, so it covers 24 bytes, and the next row of the tile starts
; exactly 24 bytes further on. Modelling the access with its full 32-byte type
; would make the two rows look like they overlap and would block promotion.

